% ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
% Part VIII: Driver
% ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
\part{The Driver}

The driver is the user-facing entry point of the compiler.  It parses
the command-line arguments, selects the requested mode of operation ---
\texttt{--dump-tokens} for lexer output, \texttt{-E} for preprocessor
output, \texttt{--dump-ast} for the parse tree, \texttt{--dump-types}
for type-annotated output, \texttt{--check} for semantic-only
validation, \texttt{--dump-ir} for the intermediate representation, or
\texttt{-c} for full compilation to an object file --- and dispatches to
the appropriate pipeline stage.  Because the compiler has no C runtime,
\texttt{\_main} is the true process entry point: it receives
\texttt{argc} and \texttt{argv} directly from the kernel's stack frame.


\begin{multicols}{2}
@i literate/driver/43-main.weft
\end{multicols}
\newpage


% ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
% Part V: Verification
% ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
\part{Verification}

Trust but verify.  This part contains the test infrastructure that
guards against regressions as the compiler evolves.  The test harness
(Chapter~\ref{ch:test-harness}) provides a minimal xUnit-style
framework --- written in the same bare-metal ARM64 assembly as the
compiler itself --- with setup helpers, assertion macros, and a runner
that reports pass/fail counts to stdout.  The conformance tests
(Chapter~\ref{ch:conformance-tests}) exercise the lexer against the token
categories defined by the C17 grammar: keywords, numeric constants,
string and character literals, punctuators, comments, trigraphs, and
line splicing.  Each test feeds a known input string to the lexer and
asserts the expected token type and spelling.  The code generation tests
(Chapter~\ref{ch:codegen-tests}) take a different approach: they compile
complete C programs with \kcc{}, link the resulting object files, execute
the binaries, and verify that the exit code matches the expected value.

